every major studio has these projects  that they were extremely excited about  once  only to drop them before they ever hit  the big screen and universal pictures is  no different  from ambitious sequels to forgotten  comic book movies to a whole cancelled  universe  these are the universal movies we'll  never get to see  everyone can agree that cowboys are  awesome as are ninjas  as well as vikings well some geniuses  thought  what if they were all combined into one  wonderful megatro  that's the rough idea behind the graphic  novel cowboy ninja viking  by aj lieberman and riley rosmo the  story is about a psychotherapist who can  transform into multiple  secret agent personas that take the form  of a cowboy  a ninja and a viking chris pratt had  signed on to star as the good doctor  and game of thrones and breaking band  director michelle mclaren  would have made her feature film debut  working from a 65 million dollar budget  with a script that had been written at  various stages by  guys who'd worked on rampage the  hangover 2 and deadpool  the film had a projected release date of  june 28 2019  and it looked to be a fun action comedy  and a likely blockbuster  but just as casting was ramping up  universal pulled the movie off its  schedule  and called off production delaying the  film indefinitely  according to an insider the film had  some screenplay issues  and rumors of calling the whole thing  off bounced around for five  months before universal threw in the  towel according to a report by wired in  2017  halo publisher microsoft aggressively  tried to get a film version of its mega  popular video game series going in 2005.  the software giant took bids from  interested studios  and ultimately the only two parties left  vying for the right to make halo were  fox and universal  who decided to team up and split the  likely enormous production costs of  making a sci-fi combat film  at first things were going just fine  halo got a screenplay by 28 days later  writer alex garland  and district 9 creator neil blomkamp  signed on to direct  and that's when the clashes with the  studio began he thought he could make a  cool  cyberpunk type movie while he said  executives wanted a quote  generic boring film with the parties so  deeply at odds  halo fell apart fans still have a slim  read of hope to hold on to however  showtime announced the live action halo  series in 2020  and if that does well enough who knows  perhaps a movie might be in the cards  after all after the release of the  unnecessary but  successful jaws 2 in 1978 and the  success of the full-length disaster  movie parody airplane in 1980  john's producers david brown and richard  zaneck wondered if the same  rapid-fire joke format could be applied  to the jaws franchise  they contacted maddie simmons publisher  of iconic  70s humor magazine national lampoon and  the man behind the brand that released  animal house  simmons decided to be a producer too and  the three guys  set out to make jaws 3. or as they  hilariously called it  jaws 3 people zero the producers pursued  joe dante to direct as he just helmed  the jaw's knock-off called piranha  and they got regular lampoon  contributors todd carroll and john  hughes to write a very silly script  ultimately xanax and brown were afraid  to go into the water  as they didn't think it would be the  best idea to so thoroughly mock their  meal ticket  in the end universal did make a third  jaws movie 1983's non-humorous and  famously bad  jaws 3d hubet guillermo del toro  a modern visionary of the spooky and  surreal could adapt a classic work of  terrifying science fiction by the  legendary h.p  lovecraft at the mountains of madness is  a 1931 novella about scientists who  discover the ancient and frightening  alien mutants who live within antarctica  and making it into a movie has long been  a passion project for del toro  because of his proven track record along  with interest from tom cruise and james  cameron  universal similarly thought that at the  mountains of madness just might make a  great movie  and the studio paid for del toro to come  up with some creature designs  what the studio didn't like was del  toro's projected budget of 150 million  dollars on a project that would most  definitely earn an  r rating for its violence and general  scariness  thus limiting its box office draw by  shutting out teenage film-goers  del toro ultimately blamed himself  saying that he quote  should have lied to universal and just  told him that he'd shoot for a pg-13  ending  so as to get them to green light the  movie it remains a tantalizing missed  opportunity  and del toro has vowed that he's not  giving up on trying to get it made  former bodybuilder and california  governor arnold schwarzenegger first  proved that he could headline a movie  with the release of the epic 1982  fantasy  conan the barbarian in the film  schwarzenegger takes the classic heroes  journey as a mighty  muscle-bound sword-carrying warrior out  to avenge the death of his parents  crush your enemies see them driven  before you  and they hear the lamentation of your  women the film was a surprise hit  earning 39 million dollars at the  domestic box office  indicating a big appetite for a sequel  conan the destroyer followed in 1984  and brought in similar revenues for  universal a third movie in the series  finally got underway  about 30 years later chris morgan  screenwriter of multiple fast and  furious films  came on board with a solid premise for a  film about an  older conan and schwarzenegger was  excited by the project  however universal had a number of  concerns that morgan and others working  on the project  couldn't overcome the project remains in  limbo but in 2019  screenwriter chris morgan told the  hollywood reporter that he still had  hopes of bringing the old man conan  movie  provisionally titled the legend of conan  to theater someday  before marvel and disney assembled to  launch the marvel cinematic universe  the comics publisher contracted with  various studios to bring its superheroes  to the big screen  universal landed the rights to the  incredible hulk and with hulk in  production in late 2002  the studio was so confident that it made  agreements to make two more marvel  movies  the comic giants movie division  announced that year that universal will  be tackling one of their oldest  characters  namor the submariner and one of their  newest prime  the task of bringing the epic story of  submariner an amphibious king from  atlantis to the screen  fell to dave itself best known for  scripting the film  road to perdition meanwhile the duo of  chris conroy  and don collimay got the prime gig which  concerned a teenaged boy who could turn  into a full-grown superhero  seeing as it's been roughly 20 years  since these films were announced  during which time marvel found itself a  home at disney  submariner is likely dead in the water  and it's no longer prime's time  of course that doesn't mean they've been  entirely forgotten there's still a  chance that submariner in particular  could show up in the marvel cinematic  universe sometime very soon  who framed roger rabbit ushered in a new  era of projects that mixed live action  with animation  and helped to bring on the music video  for paula abdul's  opposites attract the song is a duet and  the male voice is credited to the wild  pair  a singing duo consisting of bruce  deshazer  and marv gunn but in the video those  vocals are synced up to the flapping  mouth of an animated cat named  mc skatcat the clip proved so popular  that virgin records gave  mc scat cat and his expanded universe of  cool feline friends  including fats taboo maestro leo  kathleen and silk a spinoff album in  1991  called mc scat cat and the stray mob  while the video for the single  scat strut performed well on mtv it  stalled at number 96 on the billboard  hot 100.  that lack of public interest is likely  what killed development of more  mcstatcat related multimedia projects  see at the peak of this minor mania  virgin music and universal pictures  discussed a big screen  mc scat cat movie that would have  blended live action and animation  it never got past the planning stages  and neither did a proposed mc  scat cat saturday morning cartoon for  fox  after disney launched the marvel  cinematic universe and warner brothers  created the dc  extended universe universal realized it  could have its own interconnected film  series too  remembering that it made classic monster  movies in the 1930s  including dracula frankenstein the  invisible man  and pride of frankenstein among other  classics universal decided to reboot and  link those films together  in 2014 universal announced that  filmmakers alex kurtzman and chris  morgan would lead the project  which the studio ultimately named the  dark universe in 2017.  along with that news universal said it  would produce bride of frankenstein  directed by bill condon  and scheduled for release on february 19  2019  that would be followed by movies with  javier bardem as frankenstein's monster  johnny depp is the invisible man and  russell crowe is dr jekyll and mr hyde  but death is a doorway and the past  cannot remain buried forever  and none of these movies happened why  well blame the mummy this early dark  universe  entry earned savage reviews and a so so  money losing 80 million dollars at the  domestic box office  a few months later kurtzman and morgan  left the dark universe  and the studio postponed bride of  frankenstein from its 2019 release  saying in a statement that the film  needed quote more time to develop  nevertheless in january 2019 universal  proclaimed that the dark universe was  over  but said that it would continue to  develop some of those monster movies  into standalone films  in early 2020 we saw the first fruits of  those labors  when the invisible man starring  elizabeth moss arrived in theaters to  positive reviews and a strong box office  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

